WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.321
A segment tree divides an array recursively into power-of-two subsegments stored in a binary tree.

00:00:07.321 --> 00:00:16.361
An iterative segment tree places leaves at indices N through 2N minus one and internal parents at index i divided by two.

00:00:16.361 --> 00:00:20.320
This flat layout avoids recursion overhead in Python.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:27.239
To update a single element, write the new value at its leaf position and walk upward to the root.

00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:32.236
At each parent, recompute the aggregate from its left and right children.

00:00:32.236 --> 00:00:36.000
Only the O(log N) ancestors along the path are touched.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:42.561
To query an arbitrary range, start at the leaf boundaries and climb toward the root from both sides.

00:00:42.561 --> 00:00:50.491
Whenever a left boundary is a right child or a right boundary is a left child, fold that node into the answer and step inward.

00:00:50.491 --> 00:00:53.387
At most two nodes are combined per tree level.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:01:02.200
Segment trees work with any associative operation, including minimum, maximum, greatest common divisor, or matrix products.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:08.027
Define the identity element carefully so empty sub-queries never corrupt the result.

00:01:08.027 --> 00:01:12.398
Use lazy propagation when whole ranges must be updated at once.
